@pray-more
go-to: the-end

You squeeze your eyes shut and try to bargain. You've given your best to this vocation of yours. All you had to give, at any rate. Maybe the final step has to be grace?

But nothing happens. It doesn't come to you. You can ask for origin language, pronunciation again, use in a sentence, but that word isn't coming.


@lets-go
view-if: highest-win = 0

To start, you're back at the local school. It's a little embarrassing that you've never gotten past this level, but if you're lucky, maybe this year you'll get further.

To avoid getting out, you must spell

- @narsissistic: NARSISSISTIC
- @narsussistic: NARSUSSISTIC
- @narcissistic: NARCISSISTIC
- @narcessistic: NARCESSISTIC

@lose-3
choose-if: spelling < 50 
on-arrival: month = 1; age += 1
unavailable-subtitle: Or that.

"PUZSTA."

It turns out you have the Z and the S backwards. That's it. That's all. The other way around and you could have been the national spelling champion of the entire United States, with $30,000 in prize money and newspaper articles written about you. But you didn't.


